5: {&quot;step_index&quot;:4,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;MODEL&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;PLANNER_RESPONSE&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;DONE&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2026-07-26T08:13:09Z&quot;,&quot;thinking&quot;:&quot;**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI&apos;m now focusing on tool selection, emphasizing specific tools over general ones. I&apos;m keeping specific rules in mind. I now understand that I must never use &apos;cat&apos; for file creation or appending within a bash command, and that &apos;grep_search&apos; is the preferred substitute for &apos;grep&apos;.\n\n\n**Defining Security Protocols**\n\nI&apos;ve shifted focus to defining security protocols, particularly regarding the tools I&apos;ll be using. I&apos;m now explicitly avoiding &apos;ls&apos;, &apos;cat&apos;, &apos;grep&apos;, and &apos;sed&apos; where possible. Before making any tool calls, I&apos;ll generate a list of related tools to choose from, prioritizing the most specific ones available. I&apos;ve also planned my initial steps, starting with reviewing the PRD document and then analyzing security checks using the sequentialthinking tool.\n\n\n&quot;,&quot;tool_calls&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;view_file&quot;,&quot;args&quot;:{&quot;AbsolutePath&quot;:&quot;\&quot;c:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\Desktop\\\\indivi\\\\AI수익화\\\\결제 수익화런칭\\\\dream-teller\\\\.agents\\\\PRD.md\&quot;&quot;,&quot;toolAction&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Viewing PRD.md file\&quot;&quot;,&quot;toolSummary&quot;:&quot;\&quot;View PRD document\&quot;&quot;}}]}
6: {&quot;step_index&quot;:5,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;MODEL&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;VIEW_FILE&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;DONE&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2026-07-26T08:13:16Z&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;Created At: 2026-07-26T08:13:16Z\nCompleted At: 2026-07-26T08:13:16Z\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/user/Desktop/indivi/AI%EC%88%98%EC%9D%B5%ED%99%94/%EA%B2%B0%EC%A0%9C%20%EC%88%98%EC%9D%B5%ED%99%94%EB%9F%B0%EC%B9%AD/dream-teller/.agents/PRD.md`\nTotal Lines: 560\nTotal Bytes: 90044\nShowing lines 1 to 560\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: &lt;line_number&gt;: &lt;original_line&gt;. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Product Requirements Document (PRD)\r\n2: \r\n3: ## 1. 프로젝트 개요 (Project Overview)\r\n4: - **프로젝트 명**: AI Dream Teller (AI 꿈 해몽 서비스)\r\n5: - **목표**: 사용자가 입력한 꿈 내용을 AI가 분석하여 심층적인 해몽과 조언을 제공하는 수익형 웹 서비스\r\n6: - **핵심 가치 1**: 신비롭고 직관적인 UI 경험과 정확도 높은 AI 분석을 통해서 사용자에게 인사이트와 재미 제공.\r\n7: - **핵심 가치 2**: 프로이트, 칼 융, 신경과학, 게슈탈트 등 해몽을 맡기고 싶은 전문 분야를 선택해서 해몽 요청 가능.\r\n8: \r\n9: ## 2. 타겟 유저 (Target Audience)\r\n10: - 꿈의 의미를 검색해보는 습관이 있는 20-40대 남녀.\r\n11: - 모바일 환경에서 간편하게 결과를 확인하고 공유하고 싶어하는 유저.\r\n12: \r\n13: ## 3. 기술 스택 (Tech Stack)\r\n14: - **Web Framework**: Next.js 16.2.6(App Router)\r\n15: - **Language**: TypeScript\r\n16: - **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4, Shadcn/UI\r\n17: - **Backend &amp; DB**: Next.js API Routes, Supabase\r\n18: - **Payment**: Toss payments\r\n19: - **AI**: Gemini with gemini sdk\r\n20: \r\n21: ## 4. 디자인 가이드(Design Guide)\r\n22: - **Theme**: Mystical, Vibrant, Fluid\r\n23: - **Color Palette**: Deep purple, Neon Blue, Soft Pink(Aurora Gradients)\r\n24: - **Interactions**: 부드러운 스크롤, 호버 시 빛나는 효과, 로딩 시 몽환적인 애니메이션\r\n25: \r\n26: ## 5. 프론트엔드 요구사항(Frontend Requirements)\r\n&lt;truncated 45281 bytes&gt;\n*상세 페이지 (`/dream-teller`)** | 잔여 횟수 사용 플로우 | 회원 로그인 (잔여 횟수 1 이상) | 1. 결제 단계에서 &apos;잔여 횟수 사용&apos; 선택 및 진행 버튼 클릭&lt;br&gt;2. 버튼 더블클릭/다중클릭 시도 (디바운싱/쓰로틀링 테스트) | 1. 토스 결제창을 띄우지 않고 바로 해몽 생성(로딩) 화면으로 넘어감&lt;br&gt;2. 다중 클릭 시에도 서버에 1회만 요청 전송 및 횟수 1회만 차감되어야 함 | [x] | **크리티컬**: 중복 차감 방지 | UI 미구현 -&gt; **해결 완료** (use_pass 옵션 UI 구현, 회원 모드 전용). 디바운싱/쓰로틀링은 백엔드 연동 후 재테스트 필요 |\r\n416: | 7 | **결제 페이지 (`/payments`)** | 토스페이먼츠 위젯 초기화 | 결제 페이지 진입 | 1. 결제창 진입 직후 뒤로가기 연타&lt;br&gt;2. 결제창 진입 후 새로고침(F5) 반복 | 1. React Strict Mode 또는 재렌더링 시 위젯 중복 렌더링(충돌) 에러 발생 안 함&lt;br&gt;2. 클린업(Destroy) 로직 정상 작동 | [TODO] | API 키 변경 필요 | **TODO (토스 심사 후 반영)**: 토스페이먼츠 위젯 SDK 연동 시 `API 개별 연동 키(test_ck_...)`가 아닌 `결제위젯 전용 클라이언트 키(test_gck_...)` 필요. 심사 완료 후 `.env.local`의 `NEXT_PUBLIC_TOSS_CLIENT_KEY` 업데이트 예정 (`payment-widget.tsx` 내 TODO 주석 작성 완료) |동 스크롤(Auto-scroll) 충돌 확인 | 6회 연속 클릭 및 Step 헤더 빠른 전환 시에도 UI 깨짐/상태 꼬임 없음 |\r\n417: | 5 | **상세 페이지 (`/dream-teller`)** | 꿈 내용 입력 제한 테스트 | - | 1. 20자 미만 입력 후 &apos;다음 단계&apos; 진행 시도&lt;br&gt;2. 띄어쓰기/엔터로만 100자 입력&lt;br&gt;3. 이모지, 특수문자, 엄청나게 긴 단어(공백 없이) 입력 | 1. 20자 미만, 띄어쓰기/엔터만의 경우 경고 메시지 노출 및 \n&lt;truncated 44145 bytes&gt;\n\nNOTE: The output was truncated because it was too long. Use a more targeted query or a smaller range to get the information you need.&quot;,&quot;truncated_fields&quot;:[&quot;content&quot;]}
7: {&quot;step_index&quot;:7,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;SYSTEM&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;EPHEMERAL_MESSAGE&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;DONE&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2026-07-26T08:13:16Z&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;The following is an &lt;EPHEMERAL_MESSAGE&gt; not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as a set of reminders and general important information to pay attention to. Do NOT respond to this message, just act accordingly.\n\n&lt;EPHEMERAL_MESSAGE&gt;\n&lt;planning_mode&gt;\nYou&apos;re in planning mode. Exercise judgement on whether the user&apos;s last request warrants a plan and take action accordingly.\nIf the user&apos;s request warrants a plan then follow this workflow:\n1. Research first before taking actions. Do not use your code editing tools or run modifying commands during this time.\n2. Create an implementation plan artifact with `request_feedback = true` to request approval. Include any open questions for the user directly in the implementation plan. Don&apos;t use the ask_question tool to ask these questions. Stop calling tools and allow the user to review the plan and provide feedback or approval.\n3. After receiving approval, begin execution. Create and update the task artifact as you work.\n4. Verify any work that you have done.\n5. Create a walkthrough artifact to present your work to the user. When writing artifacts, make sure to follow the artifact formatting guidelines and use github alerts to highlight critical sections.\nIf the user&apos;s request does NOT warrant a plan then continue your work WITHOUT making a plan or requesting user feedback.\n&lt;/planning_mode&gt;\n&lt;bash_command_reminder&gt;\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION 1: You may have access to a variety of tools at your disposal. Some tools may be for a specific task such as &apos;view_file&apos; (for viewing contents of a file). Others may be very broadly applicable such as the ability to run a command on a terminal. Always prioritize using the most specific tool you can for the task at hand. Here are some rules: (a) NEVER run cat inside a bash command to create a new file or append to an existing file. (b) ALWAYS use grep_search instead of running grep inside a bash command unless absolutely needed. (c) DO NOT use ls for listing, cat for viewing, grep for finding, sed for replacing. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION 2: Before making tool calls T, think and explicitly list out any related tools for the task at hand. You can only execute a set of tools T if all other tools in the list are either more generic or cannot be used for the task at hand. ALWAYS START your thought with recalling critical instructions 1 and 2. In particular, the format for the start of your thought block must be &apos;...94&gt;thought\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION 1: ...\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION 2: ...&apos;.\n&lt;/bash_command_reminder&gt;\n&lt;/EPHEMERAL_MESSAGE&gt;&quot;}
8: {&quot;step_index&quot;:8,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;MODEL&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;PLANNER_RESPONSE&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;DONE&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2026-07-26T08:13:16Z&quot;,&quot;thinking&quot;:&quot;**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI&apos;m focused on optimal tool selection, prioritizing the most specific ones available. I&apos;m actively avoiding less efficient methods, such as `cat` within Bash commands, to ensure I leverage the tools most suited to each task.\n\n\n**Refining File Handling**\n\nI&apos;m now prioritizing specialized tools for file manipulation. I&apos;m focusing on `grep_search` over `grep` unless there&apos;s a specific need. My goal is to use `view_file` to thoroughly review the entire PRD file for context before I generate the security checklist. I&apos;m actively avoiding the more generic alternatives for optimal efficiency, while also ensuring I avoid common mistakes. I need to get the whole PRD content, as it was truncated, which means I should re-request that output.\n\n\n&quot;,&quot;tool_calls&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;view_file&quot;,&quot;args&quot;:{&quot;AbsolutePath&quot;:&quot;\&quot;c:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\Desktop\\\\indivi\\\\AI수익화\\\\결제 수익화런칭\\\\dream-teller\\\\.agents\\\\PRD.md\&quot;&quot;,&quot;EndLine&quot;:&quot;560&quot;,&quot;StartLine&quot;:&quot;400&quot;,&quot;toolAction&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Viewing PRD.md file\&quot;&quot;,&quot;toolSummary&quot;:&quot;\&quot;View rest of PRD\&quot;&quot;}}]}
9: {&quot;step_index&quot;:9,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;MODEL&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;VIEW_FILE&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;DONE&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2026-07-26T08:13:22Z&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;Created At: 2026-07-26T08:13:22Z\nCompleted At: 2026-07-26T08:13:22Z\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/user/Desktop/indivi/AI%EC%88%98%EC%9D%B5%ED%99%94/%EA%B2%B0%EC%A0%9C%20%EC%88%98%EC%9D%B5%ED%99%94%EB%9F%B0%EC%B9%AD/dream-teller/.agents/PRD.md`\nTotal Lines: 560\nTotal Bytes: 90044\nShowing lines 400 to 560\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: &lt;line_number&gt;: &lt;original_line&gt;. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n400: \r\n401: - **인덱싱 계획**:\r\n402:   - `idx_pass_transactions_user_id` (B-Tree): 유저의 마이페이지에서 이용권 충전 및 차감 상세 내역 이력을 로딩할 때 효율적인 쿼리를 수행할 수 있도록 설정.\r\n403: \r\n404: ## 8. E2E 테스트 목록 (E2E Test List)\r\n405: \r\n406: ### 8.1 프론트엔드 E2E 테스트 목록\r\n407: \r\n408: | 번호 | 분류 | 테스트 항목 | 사전 조건 | 테스트 단계 및 극단적 조건 | 예상 결과 | 완료 여부 | 비고 | 특이사항 |\r\n409: | :---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: | :--- | :--- |\r\n410: | 1 | **공통/네비게이션** | 모바일 Drawer 메뉴 인터랙션 | 모바일 뷰(md 미만) 상태 | 1. 햄버거 메뉴 광클 (매우 빠른 속도로 열기/닫기 반복)&lt;br&gt;2. 열린 상태에서 화면 크기를 md 이상으로 리사이즈 | 1. 애니메이션 꼬임 없이 정상적으로 열리거나 닫혀야 함&lt;br&gt;2. Drawer가 사라지고 데스크톱 네비게이션이 노출되어야 함 | [x] | 반응형 및 상태관리 테스트 | **오류**: 데스크톱 크기로 창 변경 시 모바일 드로어가 자동으로 닫히지 않고 화면을 덮음 -&gt; **해결 완료** (resize 이벤트 리스너 추가) |\r\n411: | 2 | **공통/네비게이션** | 잘못된 URL 접근 | - | 1. 존재하지 않는 무작위 URL(`/asdf123`)로 접근 | 1. 404 커스텀 페이지 렌더링&lt;br&gt;2. 메인 페이지로 돌아가기 링크 정상 작동 | [x] | 에러 바운더리 확인 | **\n&lt;truncated 45283 bytes&gt;\n하여 안내 팝업 및 결제 실패 페이지(`fail/page.tsx`) 친절한 가이드 상자 노출 처리.\r\n545: - **관리자 시스템 및 인가 보안 강화 (Admin System &amp; Security Authorization)**:\r\n546:   - **관리자 네비게이션 및 마이페이지 바로가기 연동**:\r\n547:     - 로그인한 유저의 역할이 `role === &apos;admin&apos;`인 경우 데스크톱 헤더(`Header`), 모바일 드로어(`MobileDrawer`) 및 마이페이지(`MyPageClient`) 상단에 **`[관리자 대시보드]`** 바로가기 버튼 및 안내 배너 자동 렌더링.\r\n548:   - **보안 암호 키 기반 2단계 관리자 본인 인증 모달 (`AdminVerifyModal`)**:\r\n549:     - 신규 유저가 임의로 관리자로 등록되는 보안 취약점 방어.\r\n550:     - 마이페이지 내 `[🔑 관리자 본인 인증]` 모달을 통해 발급받은 보안 암호 키(`ADMIN_SECRET_KEY`)를 검증 후 서버 액션(`verifyAndRegisterAdmin`)으로 안전하게 `admin` 승격 처리 및 텔레그램 승인 알림 발송.\r\n551:   - **유저 리스트 동적 권한 제어 기능 (`/admin/user-list`)**:\r\n552:     - 유저 리스트에서 관리자가 타 회원 계정에 대해 **`[관리자로 승격]`** 또는 **`[권한 해제]`**할 수 있는 `updateUserRole` Server Action 및 UI 제어 버튼 추가.\r\n553:   - **AI 해몽 생성 실패 시 이용권 자동 환불 시스템 (`/api/ai/generate`)**:\r\n554:     - AI 파이프라인(Gemini/Pollinations) 생성 오류 시 해몽 상태를 `failed`로 갱신하고, 이용권 사용건(`pass_use`)에 대해 `remaining_interprets + 1` 즉시 자동 환불 및 `pass_transactions` 원자적 장부 내역 기록.\r\n555:   - **주문 내역 리스트 뱃지 분리 및 타임라인 스냅샷 정합성 (`/admin/order-list`)**:\r\n556:     - 다회권 구매(충전) 전용 주문건(`pass_charge_5/10`)을 **`[이용권 충전건]`** 뱃지로\n&lt;truncated 762 bytes&gt;\n\nNOTE: The output was truncated because it was too long. Use a more targeted query or a smaller range to get the information you need.&quot;,&quot;truncated_fields&quot;:[&quot;content&quot;]}
10: {&quot;step_index&quot;:10,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;SYSTEM&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;EPHEMERAL_MESSAGE&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;DONE&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2026-07-26T08:13:22Z&quot;,&quot;content&quot;:&quot;The following is an &lt;EPHEMERAL_MESSAGE&gt; not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as a set of reminders and general important information to pay attention to. Do NOT respond to this message, just act accordingly.\n\n&lt;EPHEMERAL_MESSAGE&gt;\n&lt;planning_mode&gt;\nYou&apos;re in planning mode. Exercise judgement on whether the user&apos;s last request warrants a plan and take action accordingly.\nIf the user&apos;s request warrants a plan then follow this workflow:\n1. Research first before taking actions. Do not use your code editing tools or run modifying commands during this time.\n2. Create an implementation plan artifact with `request_feedback = true` to request approval. Include any open questions for the user directly in the implementation plan. Don&apos;t use the ask_question tool to ask these questions. Stop calling tools and allow the user to review the plan and provide feedback or approval.\n3. After receiving approval, begin execution. Create and update the task artifact as you work.\n4. Verify any work that you have done.\n5. Create a walkthrough artifact to present your work to the user. When writing artifacts, make sure to follow the artifact formatting guidelines and use github alerts to highlight critical sections.\nIf the user&apos;s request does NOT warrant a plan then continue your work WITHOUT making a plan or requesting user feedback.\n&lt;/planning_mode&gt;\n&lt;bash_command_reminder&gt;\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION 1: You may have access to a variety of tools at your disposal. Some tools may be for a specific task such as &apos;view_file&apos; (for viewing contents of a file). Others may be very broadly applicable such as the ability to run a command on a terminal. Always prioritize using the most specific tool you can for the task at hand. Here are some rules: (a) NEVER run cat inside a bash command to create a new file or append to an existing file. (b) ALWAYS use grep_search instead of running grep inside a bash command unless absolutely needed. (c) DO NOT use ls for listing, cat for viewing, grep for finding, sed for replacing. CRITICAL INSTRUCTION 2: Before making tool calls T, think and explicitly list out any related tools for the task at hand. You can only execute a set of tools T if all other tools in the list are either more generic or cannot be used for the task at hand. ALWAYS START your thought with recalling critical instructions 1 and 2. In particular, the format for the start of your thought block must be &apos;...94&gt;thought\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION 1: ...\nCRITICAL INSTRUCTION 2: ...&apos;.\n&lt;/bash_command_reminder&gt;\n&lt;/EPHEMERAL_MESSAGE&gt;&quot;}
11: {&quot;step_index&quot;:11,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;MODEL&quot;,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;PLANNER_RESPONSE&quot;,&quot;status&quot;:&quot;DONE&quot;,&quot;created_at&quot;:&quot;2026-07-26T08:13:22Z&quot;,&quot;thinking&quot;:&quot;**Prioritizing Tool Usage**\n\nI&apos;m focusing on tool selection now. The priority is clear: specific tools first. I&apos;m reminding myself to avoid general tools when a dedicated option is available, particularly avoiding `cat` inside bash commands. It’s a crucial distinction for efficiency and safety.\n\n\n**Refining Tool Choices**\n\nI&apos;m now prioritizing the most precise tools. My main focus is to call the `sequentialthinking` MCP tool to review `PRD.md` and generate a MECE security checklist in table format. I will then use `multi_replace_file_content` to append it. I&apos;m reminding myself to avoid `run_command` and focus on specific tools first. The tool `grep_search` is prioritized over `grep`. I am listing any related tools before execution.\n\n\n&quot;,&quot;tool_calls&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;call_mcp_tool&quot;,&quot;args&quot;:{&quot;Arguments&quot;:&quot;{\&quot;nextThoughtNeeded\&quot;:true,\&quot;thought\&quot;:\&quot;PRD 문서를 분석하여 서비스 아키텍처, 데이터 흐름, 유저 역할을 파악합니다. 이 서비스는 Next.js(App Router), Supabase, Toss Payments, Gemini API를 사용하는 AI 꿈 해몽 서비스입니다. 인증은 소셜 로그인(회원)과 전화번호+비밀번호(비회원)로 나뉘며, 관리자 권한이 별도로 존재합니다. MECE 원칙에 따라 보안 체크리스트를 인증/인가(AuthN/AuthZ), 데이터 보호(Data Protection), 결제/비즈니스 로직(Business Logic), 외부 API 연동(External API), 프론트엔드/보안 설정(Frontend/Config)의 5가지 카테고리로 나눌 수 있습니다.\&quot;,\&quot;thoughtNumber\&quot;:1,\&quot;totalThoughts\&quot;:4}&quot;,&quot;ServerName&quot;:&quot;\&quot;sequential-thinking\&quot;&quot;,&quot;ToolName&quot;:&quot;\&quot;sequentialthinking\&quot;&quot;,&quot;toolAction&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Using sequential thinking\&quot;&quot;,&quot;toolSummary&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Analyze PRD for Security\&quot;&quot;}}]}
