d to implement password hashing for non-member logins using Bcrypt. I&apos;m also planning to incorporate XSS and injection filtering for user input and data queries, and I&apos;m prepared to finalize data protection with RLS for core tables to ensure appropriate access controls.\n\n\n**Implementing Business Logic**\n\nI&apos;m now detailing business logic implementations. I&apos;ve focused on ensuring payment integrity by comparing client-provided amounts against DB prices, with a secondary check via TossPayments. I have also prevented multiple deductions for multi-use tickets by using DB transaction locks. I&apos;ve completed E2E and RLS validation. I am planning to implement a security measure for fraudulent refunds, which involves checking AI analysis status to prevent refunds on completed transactions. I&apos;m starting to consider LLM prompt injection and external API harmful data.\n\n\n**Confirming Key Safeguards**\n\nI&apos;m now focusing on API rate limiting and brute-force protection, especially for non-member logins and the admin authentication modal. I&apos;m planning to introduce defenses using key-value storage. Additionally, I&apos;m checking that sensitive keys like API Keys and Secrets are securely isolated on the server-side, without the `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix, to prevent environment variable exposure. I&apos;ve updated the relevant documentation tasks. I will use `multi_replace_file_content` to fix the malformed documentation in `PRD.md`. I have decided to incorporate encoding and harmful word filtering.\n\n\n&quot;,&quot;tool_calls&quot;:[{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;multi_replace_file_content&quot;,&quot;args&quot;:{&quot;Description&quot;:&quot;\&quot;PRD에 MECE 보안 체크리스트를 표 형식으로 추가했습니다.\&quot;&quot;,&quot;Instruction&quot;:&quot;\&quot;Add MECE Security Checklist at the end of PRD.md\&quot;&quot;,&quot;ReplacementChu
